+/**
+ * Chips: a finished animation ends once this frame's flush has mounted where it came to rest. Its
+ * last progress and its end came in the same frame, before the flush, and the flush passes over an
+ * animation that has ended, so its last frame was never mounted. With every frame on time the frame
+ * before is a fraction of a point short; with the UI thread held up past the end, the view stayed
+ * where the frame before left it: the field opening into its list stuck part grown, the list running
+ * down over it (ADR 0256's addendum). Finalizers run in order, and this frame's flush was asked for
+ * when its progress came, so the end follows it.
